{number: 165}
{title: Give Them All to Jesus}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Are you [G] tired of chasing pretty rainbows?
Are you [D7] tired of spinning round and round?
Wrap up [G] all those shattered dreams of your life,
And at the [D7] feet of Jesus lay them [G] down.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Give them [C] all, give them all,
Give them [G] all to Jesus,
Shattered [D7] dreams, wounded hearts, and broken [G] toys;
Give them [C] all, give them all,
Give them [G] all to Jesus,
And He will [D7] turn your sorrows into [G] joy.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
He never [G] said you'd only see sunshine;
He never [D7] said there'd be no rain.
He only [G] promised a heart full of singing,
About the [D7] very things that once brought [G] pain.
{end_of_verse}
